00:31:03.690 --> 00:31:05.410
second coming from the second
component,

00:31:05.410 --> 00:31:07.690
the third coming from the third
component,

00:31:07.690 --> 00:31:11.090
all three of these lines happen
to intersect at just one point.

00:31:11.090 --> 00:31:15.630
And that point is where c equals
4 and d equals negative 3.

00:31:15.630 --> 00:31:20.690
That's telling us the amount of
each vector we need to take of x

00:31:20.690 --> 00:31:23.590
and y to make the output that we
wanted,

00:31:23.590 --> 00:31:24.250
z.

00:31:24.250 --> 00:31:26.450
