00:44:43.270 --> 00:44:47.970
We can also scale a vector by
any amount we want.

00:44:47.970 --> 00:44:49.810
A negative scalar flips its
direction.

00:44:49.810 --> 00:44:52.450
And if we take one or more
vectors,

00:44:52.450 --> 00:44:54.830
scale each one by some amount,

00:44:54.830 --> 00:44:58.580
and add the results, that's
called a linear combination.

